> (a) Do pets need to be adjacent to follow you downstairs?  I know this
> is true for one pet, but what if you have a whole zoo?  Getting them
> all around me before going downstairs might prove a bit of a
> challenge.  I haven't found a whistle or leash yet.

What you probably need to do is either choose the most valuable pets and 
leave the others behind, OR take your pets up and down levels in several 
batches: wait until some are next to you, then move down. Wait until 
they have moved away on the next level, then go back up yourself. Wait 
until some other pets are next to you, and go down again. Wait until no 
pets are next to you, then move up again. Rinse and repeat.

A magic whistle is almost imperative here, and is also almost a 
necessity when your moving on a dungeon level, since not all pets will 
be able to keep up with you around corners...

> (b) Is there a way to suppress the "you displaced your housecat"
> messages?  They seem pointless.  Yes, I'm moving and my cat moved out
> of the way...so what?

There is no way to suppress this specific message. However, if you're 
prepared to suppress several other messages as well, you could set the 
"silent" option. This will suppress various messages considered "not 
very important" by the Dev Team.

> (c) If a cat/dog/unicorn/ape eats a leprechaun corpse, do they get
> teleportitis?

Nope. Pets don't gain intrinsics other than by polymorphing into a 
monster that has these intrinsics (and will of course lose these 
intrinsics then they would assume yet another form).

